cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the tagged research-artifact release. The published article citation will be added when a final bibliographic record is available."
title: "Better synthetic individuals do not make better synthetic populations: research artifact"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "X"
    given-names: "Abdullah"
    affiliation: "Project Aware"
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullah-x-bd/LLM_Persona"
url: "https://github.com/abdullah-x-bd/LLM_Persona"
abstract: >-
  Frozen research artifact for a multi-study audit of large-language-model
  population simulation against Government of India CAMS survey respondents.
  The repository contains the canonical four-family analysis engine,
  aggregate-only final result tables, publication figures, supervised
  reference models, study provenance, and integrity checks. The central
  result is that improvements in individual-level synthetic-respondent
  fidelity do not guarantee improvements in population-level fidelity.
keywords:
  - synthetic respondents
  - synthetic populations
  - large language models
  - computational social science
  - survey simulation
  - population fidelity
  - AI evaluation
